	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Everything in this workflow comes from the cubicle command itself (cubicle alfred), so it never goes out of date: update Cubicle and the menu updates with it.

cb opens the menu. Tab opens a section:
- cb windows: every window on every workspace. Return goes to it; Tab lists where to send it, or type a name for a new workspace.
- cb go / cb send / cb snap / cb rename / cb remove, plus New Workspace from Windows, Add a Workspace, Move Workspace to Next Display and the grid.
- Anything else you type searches the menu and your windows at once.

@ and a name jumps to a workspace (@mail). w and a command snaps the window you were in (w left, w max).

The three keywords can be changed in the workflow's Configure Workflow sheet.

Needs Cubicle installed (it brings the cubicle command; run "just install" from the repo to link it to ~/.local/bin).</string>
